{
  "_comment": "Language resources for the Albani Zaria generator (scripts/albani/). Every form is written as it is spelt; the loader folds it (hooks unhooked, apostrophes unified) and matches on the same key as the text, so one spelling per word is enough unless the ASR uses two that the key does not merge. NEVER add research vocabulary here (youth, politics, Islamic-domain terms: Allah, annabi, malam, sunna, bidi'a, shari'a…): a stopword is removed from every count, and the lexicon test refuses an overlap.",
  "_hausa_provenance": "PROVISIONAL. Function words only — pronouns, tense-aspect markers, negation, particles, conjunctions, prepositions, demonstratives, numerals and the speaker's discourse fillers — picked by hand from the 400 most frequent forms of the 29 readable transcripts (October 2026). Issue #31 asks to start from Bashir, Bichi & Adamu (2024, 76 Hausa stopwords); that list could not be retrieved here and is still to be reconciled with this one. 'ainihin' and 'wato' are fillers of this speaker ('ainihin wato…'), not general Hausa stopwords. 'mata' (women / to her) and 'kasa' are deliberately absent: both carry research senses.",
