  "_layers_provenance": "Cues for the Hausa / Arabic layer classifier (scripts/albani/layers.py). The Arabic is transliterated, so script cannot separate the layers; a citation is a stretch where Hausa function words vanish and Arabic ones accumulate. 'neutral' words belong to both languages (Hausa wa 'to', fi 'more than', inna 'mother', in 'if') and count for neither side. Loans that are fully Hausa (addini, shari'a, ilimi, malami, da'awa, salafiyya) are NOT cues: they stay in the Hausa layer unless they sit inside a citation.",
